SUMMARY:Live Jazz Tuesday: Benevolent Order of the Creature\, Lodge No. 241 - Sanders\, Boyd\, Hall\, Page\, Pond & Krekel
DESCRIPTION:No one can say when the Lodge was founded\, only that the Creature was already in the corner when the columns went up\, when the paper sun was first hung and made to burn\, when the grass was cut from green stock and persuaded to grow. Four amber eyes\, arranged in no order known to symmetry\, and a patience older than the room. It does not perform. It presides. The musicians are merely the part of the night that moves. More Details \n\n\nEvery Monday and Tuesday\, Little Jumbo brings live jazz to your ears. littlejumbobar.com \n“Simply put\, Little Jumbo should be at the top of your list of places for cocktails in Asheville. The drinks and service are both top-notch\, and the atmosphere is reminiscent of a relaxed speakeasy\, without a trace of the pretention that can sometimes be found in such places.” ~ The SmokyMountains.com Local Expert Team \n 
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/live-jazz-tuesday-jay-sanders-will-boyd-zack-page-alan-hall-4-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2-2/
LOCATION:Little Jumbo\, 241 Broadway St\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
